## 1) Switch to **local day keys** everywhere you mean “user’s day”
Create a single utility and use it in both `derive.ts` and any “today” logic.

```ts
// dateKeys.ts
export function localDayKey(ms: number) {
  const d = new Date(ms);
  const yyyy = d.getFullYear();
  const mm = String(d.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, "0");
  const dd = String(d.getDate()).padStart(2, "0");
  return `${yyyy}-${mm}-${dd}`;
}

export function todayLocalKey() {
  return localDayKey(Date.now());
}
```

Then replace:
- `toISOString().slice(0,10)` usage in grouping keys
- any “todayKey()” usage

If you have persisted keys already (UTC-based), decide whether you want to migrate or just start using local keys from now on (mixing will look odd in “History”).

