## 2) Stabilize `now` and `tKey` (avoid rerender churn / recents reshuffle)
In `App.tsx`, don’t compute these directly in render.

```ts
const [now, setNow] = useState(() => Date.now());
useEffect(() => {
  const id = window.setInterval(() => setNow(Date.now()), 60_000);
  return () => window.clearInterval(id);
}, []);

const [tKey, setTKey] = useState(() => todayLocalKey());
useEffect(() => {
  const id = window.setInterval(() => {
    const next = todayLocalKey();
    setTKey(prev => (prev === next ? prev : next));
  }, 60_000);
  return () => window.clearInterval(id);
}, []);
```

If you want “recents” to update faster than once/minute, you can lower the interval, but 60s is typically plenty and avoids constant reorder.

