## 3) `Escape` should only clear capture when capture has focus
Make sure you:
- only clear capture if capture input is the active element
- don’t hijack Escape from other text inputs

```ts
const isTextInputEl = (el: EventTarget | null) => {
  if (!(el instanceof HTMLElement)) return false;
  return (
    el.tagName === "INPUT" ||
    el.tagName === "TEXTAREA" ||
    el.isContentEditable
  );
};

// inside handler:
if (key === "escape") {
  const captureEl = opts.captureRef.current;
  const captureFocused = document.activeElement === captureEl;

  if (captureFocused && opts.hasCaptureText()) {
    e.preventDefault();
    opts.clearCapture();
    return;
  }

  if (isTextInputEl(e.target)) return;
  opts.collapsePanels();
}
```

This prevents “mysterious clearing” while typing elsewhere.

